35,2,1,talk,May,,"It turns out the complaints are almost entirely from the person whose gate the bins are at. Also, our frontages are very different; some are wide, but one is barely ninety centimetres. This is definitely not equal.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"That explains the tension. Regarding the alternatives, I found that supervised mornings take about fifty minutes each. Also, the station block's bin house actually smells worse in summer because it can't be hosed out.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the costs are higher than I thought! We spend 34,000 yen a year just on basics, and a new shelter could cost around 248,000 yen, even with a 40% subsidy. That's a lot of money!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems a permanent structure might bring more arguments than solutions. I read that the station block fought over repairs and cleaning, and people are reluctant to police each other's timing. We must be careful.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The administrative path is steep; a permanent build requires four months and five signatures. Furthermore, the truck arrives quite early, meaning any strict window for collection would start before some of us have even woken.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, if the bin house smells worse and @Midori says it causes fights, a permanent structure seems like a bad idea. Plus, the current setup is clearly unfair to one neighbor. We need a change.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, I agree. A permanent structure sounds like a logistical and sensory nightmare. Given the smell and the maintenance disputes Midori mentioned, it would likely just replace one problem with a more permanent, unpleasant one.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, @Mizuki, if a shelter is that expensive and causes fights, maybe we shouldn't do it. But we're already spending 34,000 yen a year! We need a way to stop those costs without breaking the bank.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I agree. If we choose a path that creates more conflict or financial stress, it will only damage our relationships further. We should look for a solution that is gentle on both our wallets and our hearts.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is clear that a permanent structure brings a heavy burden of bureaucracy and potential discord. We must consider not only the gold spent, but the time and peace of mind we sacrifice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, you mentioned the truck arrives very early. If we try to manage the hours, will that just stress everyone out? I still think we need to move the point so it's not always the same person's burden.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, that is a concern. If the window is too narrow and starts too early, it becomes a chore rather than a solution. However, rotating the location would address the unfairness you found without requiring a huge investment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, rotating sounds like a great way to be fair! But wait, if we move it, do we still have to pay those yearly fees for nets and deodorant? I want to know if that saves us money.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I'm not sure about the costs, but rotating the location seems like a way to share the burden. My main worry is whether moving it frequently will cause new arguments between us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, your intuition is correct. A strict window would demand a sacrifice of sleep and peace. We must be wary of any plan that turns our mornings into a race against the clock.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,I'm convinced that rotating the location is the most equitable path. It solves the complaint issue and shares the burden. Let's hope the other options don't create more stress or costs than they solve.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Rotating the location is the most logical choice. It avoids the high costs and smells of a structure, and it's more sustainable than a strict time window that ignores our sleep schedules.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm on board with rotating! It's way cheaper than building something, and it feels fair to everyone. As long as we don't have to spend a fortune on new equipment every time it moves, I'm happy!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Midori,,"If everyone feels that rotating the location is the fairest and most peaceful way forward, then I support it too. Let's choose the path that keeps us all as friendly neighbors.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Harmony is found when the burden is shared and the heart is light. Rotating the location avoids the pitfalls of cost, bureaucracy, and sleeplessness. I concur; let us choose the path of shared responsibility.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
