60,3,1,talk,May,,Everything we've discussed points to Option A. It's the only one that truly addresses the unfairness of the current spot without costing us a fortune or ruining our sleep. I vote for Rotating Location.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Option B is impractical due to the truck's arrival time, and Option C is too expensive and poorly maintained. Rotating the location is the most logical and sustainable choice. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for Option A too! It's the cheapest way to be fair, and I don't want us to spend hundreds of thousands of yen on a shelter that might just smell bad. Option A it is!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. Option A seems the most likely to maintain our harmony and avoid the conflicts that come with expensive repairs or policing each other's schedules. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The wisdom of the group is clear. By sharing the burden, we preserve both our resources and our relationships. I join you all in choosing the path of balance. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
